Every opioid-policy-setter should not impose a rigid-dose-standard and should not impose a rigid-duration-standard and should not impose a performance-incentive.
Every opioid-policy-setter should ensure a cautionary-threshold-policy that does not cause a rapid-opioid-taper.
Every opioid-policy-setter should ensure a cautionary-threshold-policy that does not cause an abrupt-opioid-discontinuation.
Every opioid-policy-setter should not penalize a clinician during a high-dosage-patient-acceptance.
Every opioid-policy-setter should not penalize a clinician that does not rapidly taper a long-term-opioid-medication for a patient.
